# Copy this file to .env.local (which is gitignored) and fill in your real
# values from the Supabase project dashboard -- Settings -> API.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars are intentionally public: this is the same anon/public
# key already embedded in the old app.js (see src/lib/supabase.ts). It is
# meant to be visible client-side -- security is enforced by Supabase's Row
# Level Security policies, not by hiding this key. Never put the
# service_role key in a NEXT_PUBLIC_* var; it would ship to every visitor's
# browser.
   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://sddanngxqjqgjnfxpmlf.supabase.co
   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_zF3ZhpG5tNx8MKHR46GNjw_kgwIimkW
# Optional -- only needed once you have a real domain. Used for sitemap.xml,
# robots.txt, and Open Graph/canonical URLs (see src/lib/site.ts). Without
# it, those fall back to Vercel's own preview/production URL automatically,
# or http://localhost:3000 when running locally -- so this is safe to leave
# unset until you're ready to point a custom domain at the Vercel project.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://uidive.example.com